< {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"status","title":"Logic Pro status","description":"Whether Kumi's bridge in Logic Pro is connected: the Logic Pro and bridge versions, the open project, and whether Logic Pro is busy (a dialog, a render). With several Logic Pro instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."}},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"discover","title":"Find running Logic Pro","description":"Every running Logic Pro with Kumi's bridge: process id, port, resource folder, versions, open project, and whether it answers. Use it when status reports none, or to choose among several.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{},"additionalProperties":false},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false}},{"name":"read","title":"Read Logic Pro","description":"Rows of one kind from the open Logic Pro project, a page at a time: {items, nextCursor?, epoch}. Pass parent (a row's ref) to read what is inside it, such as a track's items or an FX's parameters; pass the previous page's nextCursor as cursor for the next page. Or pass ref alone for the one object it names. Refs hold until the epoch changes. With several Logic Pro instances running, pass pid or resource from discover.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"pid":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"The Logic Pro process to use, from discover, when several run."},"resource":{"type":"string","description":"The Logic Pro to use, by its bundle id (com.apple.logic10) from discover, when several run."},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["project","track","region","not